From 4fcc05ff0b0b8cf74e7881f8a50ed0b1d29f193a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fawad haider <153737+FawadHa1der@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:33:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Port Verbose (feature/more-induction) to Lean 4.34 /
 Mathlib v4.34.0
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Against Mathlib 5ed2965 (v4.34.0), compiled with the toolchain release's
native compiler (lean-v4.34.0-e1a79c1 native64); all 54 modules build,
including the #guard_msgs tests of the help output.

- GCongr: `GCongrM.run` now returns the whole `GCongr.State`; the
  unsolved goals are its `newGoals` (Common.tryGcongrComputeLemmas,
  Since).
- Set notation: Mathlib v4.34 elaborates `s ⊆ t` on sets and finsets
  to `s ≤ t` (Mathlib.Tactic.SetNotationForOrder; it only prints as
  `⊆`) and Set has no `HasSubset` instance any more. Without a fix the
  help tactic described set inclusions as inequalities ("s ≤ t", the
  `#guard_msgs` test in HelpInfrastructure caught it) and the subset
  help extensions never fired.
  * `Lean.Expr.usesSetNotation`: an order relation on a type with a
    `UsesSetNotationForOrder` instance.
  * `relInfo?` gives " ⊆ " for `≤` there and nothing for `<`, `≥`, `>`
    (`⊂`, `⊇`, `⊃` were plain propositions before, as they stay).
  * `parse` reads such a `≤` as `.subset`.
  * the subset hyp/goal help extensions are keyed on every `≤` (they
    act only on `.subset`) and on `HasSubset.Subset` for other types.
- Statements: `ToSnapshotTree` is built in `ToSnapshotTreeM` (as core's
  `MacroExpandedSnapshot`).
- HelpInfrastructure: `pushTac` expands to `Bind.bind q pushTactic`
  (4.34 parses `(← $q)` in a `do` quotation as a doElem).
- lean-toolchain: v4.34.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
